  "shared_key_variants": {
    "text.1f5087db919c": "Codex reviewed this distinction at the maintainer's request: 01b-react translates the learner-visible log label 'question' as '問題'; 01c-tools and 02b-rag retain 'question' as an executable tool-schema field name.",
    "text.c4b2896a2081": "02a-routing closes the ASCII '(finish_reason: ' diagnostic with ').'; 04a-safety closes the translated full-width opening parenthesis after the allowed-destination count with '）。'. Each value preserves its own displayed sentence's paired punctuation. This records a contextual resource distinction, not publication acceptance.",
    "text.cdb4ee2aea69": "Independent Codex language review under the maintainer-authorized integration preserved the full-width sentence stop after the 02c-deep worker context, previously part of the translated context-and-write_file instruction. The filename sentence and other executable diagnostic sentences retain ASCII periods. These are reviewed prompt punctuation variants; they do not alter a path, enum or protocol value."
  },
